course: dictionary
lesson: 1786
title: Words that sound like their meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like what they mean. Say clink out loud and you can almost hear a short, light ringing sound. Context helps you check this.
explain: «At last, right above their heads, they hear cheering, stamping and glasses clinking — the weasels' party.» The cheering and stamping show it is a party, and glasses clinking means glasses making that light ringing sound as people celebrate.
explain: Clink can also be a verb, something you do. To clink is to make that sound, or to touch glasses together. Try your meaning in the sentence: "they hear glasses touching together and ringing" still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: A clink is a short, light ringing sound, like glasses touching or coins falling.
fact: To clink means to make that sound, or to touch glasses together.
fact: «Clinking» is the -ing form of the verb, so «glasses clinking» means glasses making that sound right now.
fact: People clink glasses at parties to celebrate, which is why the sound fits a party scene.
fact: «The clink» is an old slang word for prison, so one word can have very different meanings.
exercise: «At last, they hear glasses clinking.» What does clinking mean here? | A long, low hum | A loud crash of breaking plates | *A short, light ringing sound | A soft purring, like a cat
exercise: Which of these sounds is a clink? | *Two coins dropping into a jar | Thunder rolling across the sky | A deep drum beat | A heavy book thudding onto a desk
exercise: Find and copy the word that means touched glasses to make a ringing sound: «The friends clinked their glasses.» | cheers | glasses | friends | *clinked
test: «They clinked their glasses to celebrate.» What does clinked mean? | Put them away in a cupboard | *Touched glasses together so they ring | Dropped them on the floor and broke them | Filled them right to the top
test: Which meaning of clink is an old slang word? | To touch glasses together | *Prison | A coin in a piggy bank | A short, light ringing sound
exam: The keys ___ together in her pocket as she ran to the door. | Glowed | Melted | Whispered | *Clinked
